      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_87d664f423ce73172dfa09714af75e480e7773f27cc8a45f5f5773ab41982026",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Positive orthogonality explains interlacing for three-term recurrences but does not extend unchanged to four-term recurrences: the normalized C>=3 family is proved interlacing by a separate transition argument, whereas an explicit Hermite-based positive functional can be fitted to a four-term recurrence whose fourth polynomial has a nonreal zero.",
