    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_97b4922152766997eb9bca80fd6ca86749ee52082c6a9f171a706a8785526793",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Here 'Riemann hypothesis' denotes a finite polynomial zero-location analogy: symmetry under s->1-s motivates zeros on Re(s)=1/2, substitutions turn that question into real-zero and interlacing problems for recurrence polynomials, and renormalization produces parameter-threshold conjectures together with the proved sufficient regime C>=3 for one normalized four-term family.",
